@startuml M6-Deployment-Architecture

' Shows how the distributed search engine is deployed across multiple nodes in a cluster
' Includes all M1-M5 infrastructure: Serialization, TCP networking, Gossip protocol, sharded KV store, MapReduce
' Local development setup: 4 nodes running in parallel with consistent hashing to distribute data
' Search/crawl/index phases run as separate processes that communicate through distributed store

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
!define ACCENTCOLOR #1F77B4
!define ACCENTCOLOR2 #FF7F0E

skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam componentFontColor #333
skinparam ArrowColor #666

title M6 Distributed Search Engine - Deployment Architecture

cloud "GitHub.com" {
  component [GitHub API] as GITHUB
}

package "Seed Layer" {
  component [seed repositories\n(github-repos.txt)] as SEEDS
}

package "Local Development (M1-M5 Runtime)" {
  
  package "Network Layer (M2)" {
    component [TCP Socket\nServer] as SOCKET
    component [RPC Server] as RPC
  }
  
  package "Gossip Protocol (M3)" {
    component [Member Discovery] as DISCOVER
    component [Message Broadcast] as BROADCAST
    component [Failure Detection] as FAILDETECT
  }
  
  package "Serialization (M1)" {
    component [Message\nSerialization] as SERIAL
  }
  
  package "Distributed Store (M4)" {
    component [Key-Value Store\nNode 1] as KV1
    component [Key-Value Store\nNode 2] as KV2
    component [Key-Value Store\nNode 3] as KV3
    component [Consistent\nHashing] as HASH
  }
  
  package "MapReduce Engine (M5)" {
    component [Job Coordinator] as COORD
    component [Map Workers] as MAPW
    component [Reduce Workers] as REDW
    component [Task Scheduler] as SCHED
  }
}

package "Search Engine Processes" {
  
  package "Crawl Process" {
    component [Seed Loader] as SL
    component [Repository Parser] as RP
    component [GitHub Fetcher] as GF
  }
  
  package "Index Process" {
    component [Document\nProcessor] as DOCPROC
    component [Index Builder] as INDEXBUILD
    component [Term Frequency\nCalculator] as TFC
  }
  
  package "Search Process" {
    component [Query Parser] as QP
    component [Searcher] as SEARCHER
    component [Ranking Engine] as RANKER
  }
  
  package "CLI Layer" {
    component [search-cli] as SEARCHCLI
    component [Result\nFormatter] as FORMATTER
  }
}

'' External Communication
SEEDS --> SL: Repository list
SL --> RP: Parse seeds
RP --> GF: Fetch metadata
GF --> GITHUB: API calls

'' M4 Store Architecture
HASH --> KV1: Routes requests
HASH --> KV2: Routes requests
HASH --> KV3: Routes requests

KV1 -.-> KV2: Replication
KV2 -.-> KV3: Replication

'' M2/M3 Network
SOCKET --> SERIAL: Network messages
RPC --> SERIAL: RPC calls
DISCOVER --> BROADCAST: Gossip
FAILDETECT --> BROADCAST: Health updates

'' Crawl Phase
GF --> DOCPROC: Repository documents
DOCPROC --> HASH: Store documents
COORD --> MAPW: Distribute crawl tasks

'' Index Phase
DOCPROC --> INDEXBUILD: Processed documents
INDEXBUILD --> TFC: Build term frequencies
TFC --> HASH: Store inverted index
INDEXBUILD --> HASH: Store TF/DF data
COORD --> MAPW: Distribute index tasks

'' Search Phase
SEARCHCLI --> QP: User query
QP --> SEARCHER: Parsed query
SEARCHER --> HASH: Lookup index
SEARCHER --> RANKER: Candidate documents
RANKER --> FORMATTER: Ranked results
FORMATTER --> SEARCHCLI: Formatted output

'' Communication
DOCPROC -.-> SERIAL: Serialize documents
SEARCHER -.-> SERIAL: Serialize requests
HASH -.-> SERIAL: Message format

note right of HASH
  Consistent hashing
  distributes index
  across K V3 nodes
end note

note right of COORD
  For large datasets,
  crawl and index phases
  can be parallelized
  via MapReduce
end note

note right of SOCKET
  M2 TCP socket server
  enables remote
  communication
end note

note right of DISCOVER
  M3 gossip protocol
  maintains cluster
  membership info
end note

package "Storage" {
  database [Local Cache\n(.cache/)] as CACHE
  database [Results\n(benchmarks/results/)] as RESULTS
  database [Sample Data\n(data/)] as DATA
}

HASH --> CACHE: Persistent backup
FORMATTER --> RESULTS: Benchmark results
SEEDS --> DATA: Fixture data

@enduml
